<title>NETHERLANDS: REED-ELSEVIER BUYS FRENCH FIRM.</title>
<headline>REED-ELSEVIER BUYS FRENCH FIRM.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Dutch publishing group Reed-Elsevier said on Tuesday its French subsidiary Editions du Juris-Classeur had bought legal and fiscal publisher La Documentation Organique SA.    </p>
<p>The French firm is based in Paris and Strassbourg and publishes a loose-leaf legal and fiscal encyclopedia with weekly supplements.</p>
<p>La Documentation Organique has 29 employees and expects 1996 turnover of 19.3 million francs.</p>
<p>The takeover, of which no financial details were disclosed, will raise the turnover of Reed-Elsevier's French legal publishing units to about 420 million francs, the company said in a statement.</p>
